1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,439
The objet of the final Last Stage...

2
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:04,380
is colour.

3
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:08,279
Each director has to express the colour...

4
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:11,120
that has been with them from the start...

5
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:12,250
and the style of direction...

6
00:00:12,251 --> 00:00:14,066
- Only one more step to the Finals.
- They have built so far.

7
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:17,759
One director out of
three will be eliminated.

8
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:20,259
There's only one more step to the Finals.

9
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:21,859
BADA is blue.

10
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:24,829
I'm going to pour my
life's work into this stage.

11
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:26,399
I want to give off good
energy with my art...

12
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,829
and make the world green around me.

13
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:30,769
I want to try something new.

14
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:33,840
I thought of bruises when I
thought of the colour purple.

15
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:36,250
I have to go to the Finals no matter what.

16
00:00:36,310 --> 00:00:38,709
I might be eliminated if this continues.

17
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:40,909
One director will have
to end their journey...

18
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:43,650
so close to the Finals.

19
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:46,420
Who will be the director...

20
00:00:47,350 --> 00:00:49,890
to make it past the
final "Last Stage: 24H"?

21
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:52,219
Ready, fight!

22
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,890
(The finalists will be determined today.)

23
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,560
("Street World Fighter: Directors' War")

24
00:00:57,730 --> 00:00:58,900
(Last Stage: 24H)

25
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:07,240
("Last Stage: 24H")

26
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:11,080
There are only 24 hours given.

27
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:16,480
A battle for the Finals.

28
00:01:16,966 --> 00:01:19,066
"Last Stage: 24H".

29
00:01:21,306 --> 00:01:25,106
The two finalists will be determined today.

30
00:01:25,276 --> 00:01:27,276
In the past Last Stages,

31
00:01:27,376 --> 00:01:30,576
there were tables, chairs,
cubes, and umbrellas as objets.

32
00:01:30,716 --> 00:01:32,845
Each objet has been used...

33
00:01:32,846 --> 00:01:35,586
in different ways and meanings
with each director's touch.

34
00:01:35,716 --> 00:01:39,386
The final Last Stage's objet...

35
00:01:39,716 --> 00:01:41,656
is colour.

36
00:01:46,596 --> 00:01:50,466
From the Director's Room and
the colour marking their names.

37
00:01:50,566 --> 00:01:53,266
Each director has to express the colour...

38
00:01:53,396 --> 00:01:56,266
that has been with them from the start...

39
00:01:56,566 --> 00:01:58,606
and the style of direction
they have built so far.

40
00:01:59,136 --> 00:02:01,476
Three directors will...

41
00:02:01,676 --> 00:02:03,246
fill the stages with their colour.

42
00:02:03,406 --> 00:02:05,486
("Last Stage: 24H" BADA VS
Back Koo Young VS INGYOO)

43
00:02:05,646 --> 00:02:07,522
The director who has
created well-made stages...

44
00:02:07,546 --> 00:02:10,316
with extensive experience, Back Koo Young.

45
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:13,615
I'll make everyone addicted to
Back Koo Young's performance.

46
00:02:13,616 --> 00:02:15,185
I have to make it to the Finals.

47
00:02:15,186 --> 00:02:18,356
The director who utilizes her
powerful presence on stage...

48
00:02:18,526 --> 00:02:21,526
to create a unique identity, BADA.

49
00:02:21,796 --> 00:02:24,396
The ace in the hole is fierce BADA.

50
00:02:24,636 --> 00:02:25,936
I'll make it out of here.

51
00:02:26,296 --> 00:02:29,435
The director who has
created his own style...

52
00:02:29,436 --> 00:02:32,236
with unique ideas and
bold attempts, INGYOO.

53
00:02:32,336 --> 00:02:35,176
I want to create a cool
stage that brings people joy.

54
00:02:35,306 --> 00:02:37,675
Who will be the directors...

55
00:02:37,676 --> 00:02:40,016
who keep their colour
and name until the end?

56
00:02:40,176 --> 00:02:44,216
The final "Last Stage: 24H" begins now.

57
00:02:44,486 --> 00:02:46,586
Ready? Fight!

58
00:02:49,556 --> 00:02:52,156
(Who will be the director
to make it to the Finals?)

59
00:02:57,636 --> 00:02:59,136
I feel strange.

60
00:02:59,836 --> 00:03:00,836
(Tutting)

61
00:03:01,136 --> 00:03:04,006
I think my personal colour is Last Stages.

62
00:03:04,176 --> 00:03:05,275
I'm even excited.

63
00:03:05,276 --> 00:03:06,906
(Laughing)

64
00:03:06,936 --> 00:03:09,706
(Chuckling)

65
00:03:10,516 --> 00:03:12,276
This is a bit of a shock to me.

66
00:03:12,876 --> 00:03:14,346
A big shock to me.

67
00:03:15,246 --> 00:03:16,545
Goodness.

68
00:03:16,546 --> 00:03:18,262
(This is Back Koo Young's
first time in The Last Stage.)

69
00:03:18,286 --> 00:03:19,486
I didn't see this coming.

70
00:03:20,556 --> 00:03:21,725
(Glancing)

71
00:03:21,726 --> 00:03:23,155
Gosh, wait a minute!

72
00:03:23,156 --> 00:03:24,495
(Back Koo Young and BABYZOO locked eyes.)

73
00:03:24,496 --> 00:03:25,525
He looked at me.

74
00:03:25,526 --> 00:03:27,625
Koo Young just glanced at me.

75
00:03:27,626 --> 00:03:29,166
(Exclaiming)

76
00:03:29,366 --> 00:03:32,195
I kept telling Koo Young he
has to go to the Last Stage...

77
00:03:32,196 --> 00:03:33,666
at least once.

78
00:03:33,766 --> 00:03:36,736
(BABYZOO kept mentioning Koo
Young going to the Last Stage.)

79
00:03:37,206 --> 00:03:39,236
Now that it really happened...

80
00:03:40,436 --> 00:03:41,506
I feel terrible.

81
00:03:42,146 --> 00:03:44,816
I sent him to the Last Stage myself.

82
00:03:47,416 --> 00:03:50,656
I saved Kasper,

83
00:03:51,456 --> 00:03:53,855
which puts the other
three in the Last Stage.

84
00:03:53,856 --> 00:03:55,986
I felt really bad.

85
00:03:57,596 --> 00:03:58,696
So it begins.

86
00:03:59,156 --> 00:04:02,366
It has been a long journey
to my first Last Stage.

87
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:05,195
It's such a shame.

88
00:04:05,196 --> 00:04:08,106
But this is the first
time I'm feeling this way.

89
00:04:08,366 --> 00:04:11,236
(Back Koo Young has gotten
good results for each mission.)

90
00:04:11,276 --> 00:04:13,776
(Final director of the Title
Sequence Film Mission)

91
00:04:14,176 --> 00:04:16,706
(He won the K-pop Solo
Artist Direct Mission.)

92
00:04:16,846 --> 00:04:18,246
(Back Koo Young, 2nd place)

93
00:04:18,716 --> 00:04:22,286
(2nd place in the Super
Kids Dancer Casting Battle)

94
00:04:22,516 --> 00:04:25,256
I was on a winning streak,

95
00:04:25,986 --> 00:04:28,986
and I got my first taste of bad luck.

96
00:04:29,386 --> 00:04:31,386
It reminded me of my
days in "Street Man Fighter".

97
00:04:31,456 --> 00:04:33,866
I've never gone to the elimination round...

98
00:04:33,966 --> 00:04:35,826
until the semi-final round.

99
00:04:36,196 --> 00:04:39,596
I lost at the very end and
couldn't make it to the Finals.

100
00:04:39,936 --> 00:04:41,166
That's why I'm on this show.

101
00:04:42,836 --> 00:04:46,076
I didn't want to make that
same mistake ever again.

102
00:04:46,206 --> 00:04:47,306
I have to prove myself.

103
00:04:47,406 --> 00:04:49,846
I'll show them why those
who last long are strong.

104
00:04:50,206 --> 00:04:52,775
I just can't accept this.

105
00:04:52,776 --> 00:04:53,776
What should I do?

106
00:04:54,816 --> 00:04:56,615
INGYOO, how about using this?

107
00:04:56,616 --> 00:04:59,616
I was actually expecting good results...

108
00:04:59,816 --> 00:05:02,185
for this direction.

109
00:05:02,186 --> 00:05:04,995
My directing skills...

110
00:05:04,996 --> 00:05:06,995
have definitely improved...

111
00:05:06,996 --> 00:05:08,695
compared to the very first mission.

112
00:05:08,696 --> 00:05:10,426
I've grown a lot.

113
00:05:10,696 --> 00:05:13,595
Everyone on set was really satisfied.

114
00:05:13,596 --> 00:05:15,236
That's great!

115
00:05:15,636 --> 00:05:17,035
I even heard...

116
00:05:17,036 --> 00:05:20,076
every moment of my stage was 10 out of 10.

117
00:05:20,206 --> 00:05:21,275
So...

118
00:05:21,276 --> 00:05:22,576
I just can't do this anymore.

119
00:05:26,676 --> 00:05:28,246
I had a meltdown.

120
00:05:30,786 --> 00:05:32,516
(Hugging)

121
00:05:32,716 --> 00:05:33,816
I can't do this anymore.

122
00:05:33,986 --> 00:05:35,186
We can do it.

123
00:05:35,326 --> 00:05:38,356
We'll be so much stronger
after we pull through.

124
00:05:38,656 --> 00:05:40,455
- You never know.
- That's true.

125
00:05:40,456 --> 00:05:42,065
You're going to do an amazing job, right?

126
00:05:42,066 --> 00:05:45,266
I have to try at least.

127
00:05:45,396 --> 00:05:46,436
Last Stages are my things.

128
00:05:46,636 --> 00:05:49,205
I've never smiled today,
but now I can't stop.

129
00:05:49,206 --> 00:05:51,536
- You're so weird.
- I am a bit crazy.

130
00:05:53,206 --> 00:05:55,846
I think I did an amazing
job at the Last Stage before.

131
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:57,206
I've done well so far.

132
00:05:57,516 --> 00:05:59,215
This Last Stage should be fun.

133
00:05:59,216 --> 00:06:01,746
It's the first one without props.

134
00:06:02,116 --> 00:06:05,186
The objet for this Last Stage: 24H...

135
00:06:05,356 --> 00:06:06,616
- is...
- Is?

136
00:06:06,786 --> 00:06:09,186
Your own distinct colour.

137
00:06:11,056 --> 00:06:13,532
What should I do? I'll look like
a Teletubby in purple clothes.

138
00:06:13,556 --> 00:06:15,425
It's complete creative freedom.

139
00:06:15,426 --> 00:06:16,426
You're right.

140
00:06:16,427 --> 00:06:19,735
The freedom makes it more difficult,

141
00:06:19,736 --> 00:06:20,805
but I'll do good.

142
00:06:20,806 --> 00:06:23,266
I trust the future BADA will do a good job.

143
00:06:23,366 --> 00:06:25,306
This is insane. No one
has done this before.

144
00:06:25,576 --> 00:06:27,376
No one tried this is America,

145
00:06:27,646 --> 00:06:29,176
no one tried this in Korea.

146
00:06:29,376 --> 00:06:30,605
It's unprecedented.

147
00:06:30,606 --> 00:06:32,345
I'm the colour green itself.

148
00:06:32,346 --> 00:06:33,986
There's just one more step to the Finals.

149
00:06:34,016 --> 00:06:36,186
It's do or die for me.

150
00:06:36,316 --> 00:06:37,415
I'm confident.

151
00:06:37,416 --> 00:06:40,386
I'll make these 24 hours the best ones.

152
00:06:41,186 --> 00:06:42,256
Good morning.

153
00:06:44,356 --> 00:06:46,856
(Back Koo Young's team has been summoned.)

154
00:06:47,256 --> 00:06:51,166
This is the Last Stage
right before the Finals.

155
00:06:51,966 --> 00:06:54,166
What's the objet this time?

156
00:06:54,366 --> 00:06:56,506
We don't have one this time.

157
00:06:56,736 --> 00:06:57,776
- What?
- Really?

158
00:06:58,476 --> 00:07:00,176
As you can see, there's nothing here.

159
00:07:00,336 --> 00:07:01,676
There is no objet.

160
00:07:01,976 --> 00:07:04,516
The theme is each director's colour.

161
00:07:05,076 --> 00:07:07,645
- Purple?
- Purple.

162
00:07:07,646 --> 00:07:08,646
Purple!

163
00:07:08,647 --> 00:07:10,886
(1MILLION's team colour
in "Street Man Fighter")

164
00:07:10,986 --> 00:07:13,626
(Back Koo Young's colour in "Street
World Fighter: Directors' War")

165
00:07:13,756 --> 00:07:15,785
We used 1MILLION's team colour.

166
00:07:15,786 --> 00:07:17,356
Exactly. Purple.

167
00:07:17,996 --> 00:07:20,195
After they told us the theme,

168
00:07:20,196 --> 00:07:23,295
I thought of bruises when I
thought of the colour purple.

169
00:07:23,296 --> 00:07:24,795
We get bruised up a lot.

170
00:07:24,796 --> 00:07:25,935
It's impossible not to.

171
00:07:25,936 --> 00:07:27,435
- You all have them now, - Yes.

172
00:07:27,436 --> 00:07:29,005
- somewhere.
- Right.

173
00:07:29,006 --> 00:07:31,175
NEMO, you remember. For
the 1-on-1 Signature Mission,

174
00:07:31,176 --> 00:07:33,476
I kept throwing Bambi on the floor.

175
00:07:34,106 --> 00:07:38,176
On stage, I grabbed Bambi's
hand and threw her on the ground.

176
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:39,945
On the night of the performance,

177
00:07:39,946 --> 00:07:42,115
I saw a bruise on Bambi's shoulder...

178
00:07:42,116 --> 00:07:44,156
that was around this size.

179
00:07:44,286 --> 00:07:45,316
Right here.

180
00:07:45,656 --> 00:07:47,186
She kept hitting the floor here.

181
00:07:47,456 --> 00:07:51,156
She had a very big, purple
bruise on her shoulder.

182
00:07:51,896 --> 00:07:53,026
I just...

183
00:07:53,596 --> 00:07:54,666
It's nothing!

184
00:07:54,866 --> 00:07:55,896
I'm to blame.

185
00:07:55,926 --> 00:07:58,366
- No, you're not!
- That's not true!

186
00:07:58,466 --> 00:08:00,366
We get hurt all the time.

187
00:08:00,836 --> 00:08:02,435
I was reminded of that moment...

188
00:08:02,436 --> 00:08:03,906
as soon as I thought of purple.

189
00:08:04,576 --> 00:08:07,035
I think I bruised each dancer...

190
00:08:07,036 --> 00:08:09,806
at least five times with my choreography.

191
00:08:10,176 --> 00:08:12,975
I felt terrible but so
grateful at the same time.

192
00:08:12,976 --> 00:08:14,192
(Back Koo Young gifted the
dancers knee pads as a thank you.)

193
00:08:14,216 --> 00:08:16,385
- Did you put your knee pads on?
- Yes!

194
00:08:16,386 --> 00:08:18,186
- You have your knee pads on, right?
- Yes!

195
00:08:18,316 --> 00:08:20,615
I wanted to express...

196
00:08:20,616 --> 00:08:22,456
that even if we get bruised...

197
00:08:22,556 --> 00:08:23,956
over and over again,

198
00:08:24,096 --> 00:08:26,055
we won't be able to stop dancing...

199
00:08:26,056 --> 00:08:27,355
with the theme of poison.

200
00:08:27,356 --> 00:08:29,996
So our concept for this
stage is bruises and poison.

201
00:08:30,196 --> 00:08:33,035
Even if we have purple bruises all over us,

202
00:08:33,036 --> 00:08:34,605
we keep the performance going.

203
00:08:34,606 --> 00:08:36,735
It's kind of like being
addicted to dancing.

204
00:08:36,736 --> 00:08:39,236
So I decided to use purple poison as well.

205
00:08:39,776 --> 00:08:40,806
Like this?

206
00:08:41,546 --> 00:08:44,916
The dancers will line up here,
and the smog will cover this part.

207
00:08:45,146 --> 00:08:46,215
So you want to separate
the stage with smog.

208
00:08:46,216 --> 00:08:48,916
The smog won't make it past this line.

209
00:08:49,116 --> 00:08:51,685
The smog will look like purple poison,

210
00:08:51,686 --> 00:08:53,515
and the smog won't have reached me yet.

211
00:08:53,516 --> 00:08:55,256
So I won't be poisoned in the intro.

212
00:08:55,426 --> 00:08:58,355
I tried to think of movements
that fit the concept...

213
00:08:58,356 --> 00:08:59,826
for the performance.

214
00:09:00,056 --> 00:09:03,026
I kept thinking of
things related to purple.

215
00:09:03,096 --> 00:09:06,095
Then I realised we call it a black light,

216
00:09:06,096 --> 00:09:07,836
but its actual colour is purple.

217
00:09:08,036 --> 00:09:09,165
(How Back Koo Young uses black light)

218
00:09:09,166 --> 00:09:10,205
Mix it well.

219
00:09:10,206 --> 00:09:11,575
(1. Mix red and blue ink.)

220
00:09:11,576 --> 00:09:12,635
Paint.

221
00:09:12,636 --> 00:09:13,975
(2. Paint veins with the mixed ink.)

222
00:09:13,976 --> 00:09:15,206
Now check it.

223
00:09:15,576 --> 00:09:18,046
(Poisoned purple veins complete)

224
00:09:18,416 --> 00:09:20,346
Start from my legs and go up.

225
00:09:20,416 --> 00:09:21,922
(When the dancers point the black light, )

226
00:09:21,946 --> 00:09:23,385
(the poisoned veins become visible.)

227
00:09:23,386 --> 00:09:25,815
Purple veins are used a lot in movies...

228
00:09:25,816 --> 00:09:27,585
to portray infection or a poisoned state.

229
00:09:27,586 --> 00:09:30,855
I wanted to show how
unaffected I seem on the outside,

230
00:09:30,856 --> 00:09:32,196
but how poisoned I actually am.

231
00:09:32,296 --> 00:09:34,725
I have arrived!

232
00:09:34,726 --> 00:09:36,265
I have returned!

233
00:09:36,266 --> 00:09:37,896
(Laughing)

234
00:09:38,136 --> 00:09:40,196
I can't believe I'm here again!

235
00:09:41,036 --> 00:09:43,035
It's not that scary this time.

236
00:09:43,036 --> 00:09:44,406
No umbrellas everywhere.

237
00:09:45,036 --> 00:09:46,036
(Screaming)

238
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:48,706
This is crazy.

239
00:09:49,146 --> 00:09:51,376
I'm so terrified.

240
00:09:51,616 --> 00:09:52,775
(The practice room is empty this time.)

241
00:09:52,776 --> 00:09:54,075
(What performance will be created here?)

242
00:09:54,076 --> 00:09:57,245
My colour, as you can see, is blue.

243
00:09:57,246 --> 00:09:59,285
I've been using blue since
"Street Woman Fighter 2"...

244
00:09:59,286 --> 00:10:01,556
and for "Street World
Fighter: Directors' War" too.

245
00:10:01,626 --> 00:10:02,785
(Back when she entered BEBE's blue room...)

246
00:10:02,786 --> 00:10:03,946
(in "Street Woman Fighter 2")

247
00:10:04,496 --> 00:10:05,895
(The blue is so pretty!)

248
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:06,896
(BADA entering her Director's Room...)

249
00:10:06,896 --> 00:10:07,896
(in "Street World Fighter: Directors' War")

250
00:10:07,897 --> 00:10:08,925
(It's all blue.)

251
00:10:08,926 --> 00:10:10,895
When I first made the team, BEBE,

252
00:10:10,896 --> 00:10:15,335
I wanted to keep our colour theme blue.

253
00:10:15,336 --> 00:10:18,175
It's a colour that goes with any gender,

254
00:10:18,176 --> 00:10:19,975
and it really gives fierce.

255
00:10:19,976 --> 00:10:23,646
The style of dance I prefer
is gender neutral as well.

256
00:10:23,746 --> 00:10:27,845
That's why I wanted to make
the colour blue our identity.

257
00:10:27,846 --> 00:10:29,385
And now the objet is colour?

258
00:10:29,386 --> 00:10:33,816
I thought about ways to
represent blue the best.

259
00:10:34,056 --> 00:10:38,055
I realised blue is BADA's identity itself,

260
00:10:38,056 --> 00:10:41,995
and thought this was a
way to really express myself.

261
00:10:41,996 --> 00:10:43,896
What styles are associated with me?

262
00:10:44,026 --> 00:10:47,066
Gender neutral, powerful, and cool.

263
00:10:47,296 --> 00:10:50,265
I tried to connect all of those themes...

264
00:10:50,266 --> 00:10:53,576
