connection to the sky blue colour.

770
00:30:49,836 --> 00:30:51,565
To be completely honest,

771
00:30:51,566 --> 00:30:53,476
when I saw the fur,

772
00:30:53,536 --> 00:30:55,845
I thought, "That's MIN JUN's colour."

773
00:30:55,846 --> 00:30:57,645
But through the performance,

774
00:30:57,646 --> 00:30:59,945
she really did a great job
of showing BADA's colour.

775
00:30:59,946 --> 00:31:02,516
So I thought, "I can let that pass."

776
00:31:02,646 --> 00:31:03,985
How did the three Fight Judges...

777
00:31:03,986 --> 00:31:07,086
feel about this performance?

778
00:31:07,186 --> 00:31:10,756
Let's hear the judges' evaluations.

779
00:31:10,856 --> 00:31:11,885
I believe...

780
00:31:11,886 --> 00:31:14,255
your strength...

781
00:31:14,256 --> 00:31:16,765
is clarity.

782
00:31:16,766 --> 00:31:18,595
Rather than complex composition,

783
00:31:18,596 --> 00:31:19,835
you choose very clear...

784
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:22,536
and large compositions.

785
00:31:23,206 --> 00:31:26,406
I thought it was a very
clean and sleek performance.

786
00:31:27,036 --> 00:31:28,875
I was very happy that my
work was well-received.

787
00:31:28,876 --> 00:31:32,316
I felt that my performance
was communicated effectively.

788
00:31:32,746 --> 00:31:35,116
Your choreography has points...

789
00:31:35,176 --> 00:31:37,186
that make people go crazy.

790
00:31:37,216 --> 00:31:39,956
Even just now, there were parts
that made the audience scream.

791
00:31:40,056 --> 00:31:43,356
And you know which
exact parts those will be.

792
00:31:43,456 --> 00:31:45,186
Especially in the second half.

793
00:31:45,286 --> 00:31:49,865
You really made those key parts shine...

794
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:52,095
by pacing yourself very well.

795
00:31:52,096 --> 00:31:54,736
I evaluate that very highly.

796
00:31:54,836 --> 00:31:57,166
From the starting scene,

797
00:31:57,866 --> 00:31:59,836
the choreography with the dancers,

798
00:31:59,906 --> 00:32:02,246
to you surviving at the end,

799
00:32:02,376 --> 00:32:04,805
you really did a good job of
creating a dynamic performance.

800
00:32:04,806 --> 00:32:06,016
It was so perfect.

801
00:32:06,146 --> 00:32:07,175
To be...

802
00:32:07,176 --> 00:32:09,385
extremely nit-picky...

803
00:32:09,386 --> 00:32:12,416
(Nit-picky?)

804
00:32:12,556 --> 00:32:14,685
The part where the bullet was
flying through the screen in the back.

805
00:32:14,686 --> 00:32:16,355
I think it would've been better...

806
00:32:16,356 --> 00:32:19,055
if you had drawn our eyes
to the screen before that.

807
00:32:19,056 --> 00:32:21,756
All of the dancers did look to the back,

808
00:32:21,796 --> 00:32:23,095
but I saw the bullet...

809
00:32:23,096 --> 00:32:25,736
when it was already in the middle.

810
00:32:25,796 --> 00:32:28,565
Other than that tiny thing,

811
00:32:28,566 --> 00:32:30,606
the performance was near perfect.

812
00:32:31,106 --> 00:32:33,735
I need to improve on those criticisms.

813
00:32:33,736 --> 00:32:36,646
I still do think I fully
showed everyone my colour.

814
00:32:37,276 --> 00:32:39,675
Being on stage like this,

815
00:32:39,676 --> 00:32:40,676
I'm so happy,

816
00:32:40,677 --> 00:32:41,975
and I want to do it again.

817
00:32:41,976 --> 00:32:43,015
It's so fun.

818
00:32:43,016 --> 00:32:44,896
- We want to see you again.
- Yes, like this...

819
00:32:45,346 --> 00:32:46,916
I want them to do it one more time.

820
00:32:47,316 --> 00:32:50,426
I'm so relieved that the
performance went well.

821
00:32:50,656 --> 00:32:52,326
I'm filled with emotion.

822
00:32:55,126 --> 00:32:57,595
Will BADA's colour and direction,

823
00:32:57,596 --> 00:32:59,866
filled with sky blue,

824
00:32:59,996 --> 00:33:02,635
take her to the Final Stage?

825
00:33:02,636 --> 00:33:04,765
Or will this be her last performance...

826
00:33:04,766 --> 00:33:07,606
on Street World Fighter: Directors' War?

827
00:33:07,676 --> 00:33:10,306
I used all of the strengths that I have,

828
00:33:10,346 --> 00:33:13,915
and I've created a performance...

829
00:33:13,916 --> 00:33:16,085
full of wow factors everyone will enjoy.

830
00:33:16,086 --> 00:33:18,985
I think the performance was so perfect...

831
00:33:18,986 --> 00:33:20,755
that it would be strange
for me not to survive.

832
00:33:20,756 --> 00:33:22,886
So I believe I'll survive.

833
00:33:23,856 --> 00:33:26,756
The next director who will
put on their Last Stage...

834
00:33:26,826 --> 00:33:28,356
is Back Koo Young.

835
00:33:35,766 --> 00:33:37,605
How will Director Back Koo Young...

836
00:33:37,606 --> 00:33:39,705
portray his symbolic colour, purple,

837
00:33:39,706 --> 00:33:41,235
in his performance...

838
00:33:41,236 --> 00:33:44,176
and prove his unique identity?

839
00:33:44,246 --> 00:33:46,476
Please come onto the stage.

840
00:33:48,546 --> 00:33:49,816
Dad is here.

841
00:33:51,446 --> 00:33:53,386
Doesn't he kind of seem
like a dark magician?

842
00:33:55,316 --> 00:33:57,526
I'm not really feeling purple yet.

843
00:33:58,186 --> 00:33:59,455
Director Back Koo Young.

844
00:33:59,456 --> 00:34:01,455
Please tell us how you interpreted...

845
00:34:01,456 --> 00:34:04,395
and portrayed the colour purple,
the colour that symbolizes you,

846
00:34:04,396 --> 00:34:05,636
in today's performance.

847
00:34:05,936 --> 00:34:07,195
The first thing that came to mind...

848
00:34:07,196 --> 00:34:09,906
when I heard "purple..."

849
00:34:10,006 --> 00:34:11,306
was a bruise.

850
00:34:15,006 --> 00:34:17,145
The many bruises...

851
00:34:17,146 --> 00:34:18,666
you can't avoid getting as a dancer...

852
00:34:19,046 --> 00:34:20,675
during practice...

853
00:34:20,676 --> 00:34:22,786
I'm tearing up.

854
00:34:23,246 --> 00:34:24,946
And my heart...

855
00:34:25,086 --> 00:34:27,355
that can't stop dancing...

856
00:34:27,356 --> 00:34:29,285
because I'm addicted to dance.

857
00:34:29,286 --> 00:34:31,855
I wanted to portray those
things as purple poison.

858
00:34:31,856 --> 00:34:33,395
So the title of my performance...

859
00:34:33,396 --> 00:34:34,896
is "Bruises and Poison."

860
00:34:36,366 --> 00:34:38,426
His synopsis is absolutely perfect.

861
00:34:41,396 --> 00:34:43,135
I wanted to create a look...

862
00:34:43,136 --> 00:34:45,205
that matched the story.

863
00:34:45,206 --> 00:34:47,606
We'll wear skin-tone outfits...

864
00:34:47,636 --> 00:34:51,575
and add bruises and veins using stickers.

865
00:34:51,576 --> 00:34:54,415
I wanted it to be visually clear.

866
00:34:54,416 --> 00:34:57,115
Also, the secret weapon
of this performance...

867
00:34:57,116 --> 00:34:58,545
is the ending scene.

868
00:34:58,546 --> 00:35:00,515
Veins spreading all over...

869
00:35:00,516 --> 00:35:02,455
to create the figure of a
human who is addicted.

870
00:35:02,456 --> 00:35:03,985
There's something called UV ink.

871
00:35:03,986 --> 00:35:05,725
You can't normally see it.

872
00:35:05,726 --> 00:35:08,055
We'll paint our bodies with that UV ink...

873
00:35:08,056 --> 00:35:09,525
and make it visible by using black light...

874
00:35:09,526 --> 00:35:11,895
to create the ending scene.

875
00:35:11,896 --> 00:35:13,096
That is my secret weapon.

876
00:35:13,136 --> 00:35:15,336
What is this on your face?

877
00:35:15,496 --> 00:35:17,636
It already looks so profound.

878
00:35:17,836 --> 00:35:20,176
Actually, I'm drawn to darker atmospheres.

879
00:35:20,306 --> 00:35:22,075
I wanted to bring...

880
00:35:22,076 --> 00:35:23,882
some of that dark atmosphere
with me while making the track.

881
00:35:23,906 --> 00:35:27,776
At the same time, I wanted the
track to show a clear narrative arc.

882
00:35:27,876 --> 00:35:30,985
I want the tempo to change about twice.

883
00:35:30,986 --> 00:35:34,215
So I mixed up different genres...

884
00:35:34,216 --> 00:35:36,656
for the intro, Part 2, and Part 3.

885
00:35:36,726 --> 00:35:39,425
I'd love for the tempo change...

886
00:35:39,426 --> 00:35:41,025
to come through clearly in the last part.

887
00:35:41,026 --> 00:35:42,665
I want a really fast tempo.

888
00:35:42,666 --> 00:35:44,066
When I was planning my performance,

889
00:35:44,096 --> 00:35:46,795
there were specific moments in the music...

890
00:35:46,796 --> 00:35:48,695
where I wanted to wow the audience.

891
00:35:48,696 --> 00:35:52,036
With the techno beats, the
tempo is going to pick up.

892
00:35:52,106 --> 00:35:55,376
So I needed to wow the
audience in the last part.

893
00:35:55,476 --> 00:35:57,706
The lyrics go, "There's no tomorrow."

894
00:35:58,106 --> 00:36:00,876
"There's no tomorrow. I
only live for today." That's it.

895
00:36:01,046 --> 00:36:02,315
I wanted to convey the message...

896
00:36:02,316 --> 00:36:05,955
by going up in the air and then falling.

897
00:36:05,956 --> 00:36:08,015
I wanted to use that technique
to convey the message.

898
00:36:08,016 --> 00:36:09,016
Are you okay?

899
00:36:09,226 --> 00:36:10,256
I think it will work.

900
00:36:10,356 --> 00:36:12,126
If we practice, this is going to work.

901
00:36:12,496 --> 00:36:14,125
But what happened next was the problem.

902
00:36:14,126 --> 00:36:16,166
Seven, eight. Wait.

903
00:36:20,766 --> 00:36:23,635
Given that we have
only 24 hours to practice,

904
00:36:23,636 --> 00:36:25,612
there's only a 15 percent chance
that this technique will work.

905
00:36:25,636 --> 00:36:27,505
To pull off something like that,

906
00:36:27,506 --> 00:36:30,345
I need to work with the
dancers for 4 to 5 days.

907
00:36:30,346 --> 00:36:33,245
On top of that, it's not like...

908
00:36:33,246 --> 00:36:35,076
we can keep practising for 24 hours.

909
00:36:35,216 --> 00:36:36,696
It was a reckless attempt on my part.

910
00:36:36,846 --> 00:36:39,166
It's the biggest dilemma I
have regarding the performance.

911
00:36:39,686 --> 00:36:42,186
Team Back Koo Young
will start the rehearsal.

912
00:36:42,256 --> 00:36:44,386
(He tries the jump technique
during the rehearsal.)

913
00:36:50,196 --> 00:36:51,966
Cut the music.

914
00:36:59,276 --> 00:37:00,906
Do you think you can move?

915
00:37:08,346 --> 00:37:10,145
I jumped too far ahead.

916
00:37:10,146 --> 00:37:12,226
So I couldn't catch your
back and ended up slipping.

917
00:37:12,586 --> 00:37:14,686
I can do this.

918
00:37:17,256 --> 00:37:18,256
Let me try again.

919
00:37:19,626 --> 00:37:21,126
I'll get up no matter what.

920
00:37:21,326 --> 00:37:23,396
I'll make do with what I've got.

921
00:37:24,096 --> 00:37:26,866
I'll jump off even if I
have to crawl up there.

922
00:37:29,536 --> 00:37:31,106
One, two, three, four...

923
00:37:31,166 --> 00:37:32,806
(Back Koo Young tries again.)

924
00:37:33,106 --> 00:37:35,736
Two, two, three, four, five, six...

925
00:37:40,316 --> 00:37:41,976
Cut the music.

926
00:37:42,346 --> 00:37:43,516
Let me just try the jump.

927
00:37:43,646 --> 00:37:45,115
Let me just practice the jump.

928
00:37:45,116 --> 00:37:47,816
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven...

929
00:37:49,826 --> 00:37:51,826
Okay. I'll make it work no matter what.

930
00:37:53,526 --> 00:37:56,126
Two, two, three, four, five, six...

931
00:37:58,696 --> 00:38:00,796
(However, he keeps
failing to execute the jump.)

932
00:38:02,636 --> 00:38:04,106
I was in big trouble.

933
00:38:04,566 --> 00:38:06,926
I had to stay strong and
believe that I could make it work.

934
00:38:11,046 --> 00:38:13,546
I kept failing to pull off the
jump when we were practising.

935
00:38:13,646 --> 00:38:14,716
So...

936
00:38:15,346 --> 00:38:18,186
I started to wonder if I'd
be able to pull this off...

937
00:38:18,346 --> 00:38:21,086
in front of the judges when I
only had 24 hours to prepare?

938
00:38:22,826 --> 00:38:26,426
(Spacing rehearsal)

939
00:38:29,766 --> 00:38:31,972
(He failed to pull off the jump
even during the final rehearsal.)

940
00:38:31,996 --> 00:38:33,266
That's what he's going to do?

941
00:38:33,766 --> 00:38:35,666
Things didn't look good for Koo Young.

942
00:38:36,666 --> 00:38:39,206
I think I was scared.

943
00:38:41,706 --> 00:38:42,906
"What if I mess it up again?"

944
00:38:43,706 --> 00:38:46,746
My heart pounded like
crazy right before that jump.

945
00:38:47,176 --> 00:38:49,816
I let my fear overwhelm me.

946
00:38:49,986 --> 00:38:52,986
I only pulled it off once
during my practice.

947
00:38:53,356 --> 00:38:55,816
(Final rehearsal)

948
00:38:57,326 --> 00:38:58,826
Let's go!

949
00:38:59,696 --> 00:39:02,026
- This was it?
- This was it?

950
00:39:02,326 --> 00:39:04,726
His performance definitely packs a punch.

951
00:39:04,996 --> 00:39:07,566
Will I go with the risk-free
version for the live performance?

952
00:39:08,036 --> 00:39:09,835
As long as Koo Young
doesn't make any mistakes,

953
00:39:09,836 --> 00:39:12,035
I think he's going to
get the highest score.

954
00:39:12,036 --> 00:39:14,705
If he makes a mistake
during his performance,

955
00:39:14,706 --> 00:39:16,545
it's going to affect his score a lot.

956
00:39:16,546 --> 00:39:19,546
So if he makes a mistake, he
might end up getting eliminated.

957
00:39:20,146 --> 00:39:21,906
I was thinking only
one thing at that point.

958
00:39:21,976 --> 00:39:23,936
"I'll pull this off during
my final performance."

959
00:39:24,646 --> 00:39:26,215
It wasn't, "I can do this."

960
00:39:26,216 --> 00:39:27,786
"I will just do it."

961
00:39:28,816 --> 00:39:30,085
If I can't get up there,

962
00:39:30,086 --> 00:39:32,486
I'll crawl up there. I'll
do whatever it takes.

963
00:39:33,526 --> 00:39:35,626
I really don't want to get eliminated.

964
00:39:35,896 --> 00:39:38,026
Four years ago, I was
on "Street Man Fighter."

965
00:39:38,296 --> 00:39:39,996
I got eliminated...

966
00:39:40,096 --> 00:39:42,816
at this point in the competition
and couldn't make it to the finals.

967
00:39:43,206 --> 00:39:45,206
I experienced absolute despair...

968
00:39:45,436 --> 00:39:46,906
right before the finals.

969
00:39:47,176 --> 00:39:49,176
You have no idea how much I cried that day.

970
00:39:49,376 --> 00:39:51,776
I wasn't exactly young back then.

971
00:39:52,046 --> 00:39:54,716
A huge part of me was
disappointed that I couldn't make it.

972
00:39:54,816 --> 00:39:56,845
I decided to compete on this show...

973
00:39:56,846 --> 00:39:59,192
because not making it to the
finals last time was devastating.

974
00:39:59,216 --> 00:40:01,285
I'll never be able to forget...

975
00:40:01,286 --> 00:40:03,826
how I failed to make it to the finals.

976
00:40:04,386 --> 00:40:05,386
I'm serious.

977
00:40:05,526 --> 00:40:08,355
It doesn't matter that I have a
long career as a choreographer.

978
00:40:08,356 --> 00:40:11,295
I have this ambition to keep pushing
and stay at the top of my game.

979
00:40:11,296 --> 00:40:15,495
By doing this, I gain
recognition for who I am.

980
00:40:15,496 --> 00:40:17,082
(He didn't spare his body and
did his best for every mission.)

981
00:40:17,106 --> 00:40:18,166
Thank you!

982
00:40:18,706 --> 00:40:21,706
I'm the oldest choreographer on the show.

983
00:40:23,106 --> 00:40:26,475
I know that having a
chance like this to compete...

984
00:40:26,476 --> 00:40:29,016
is rare for me.

985
00:40:29,386 --> 00:40:32,086
I wanted to show people that I still rock.

986
00:40:33,116 --> 00:40:35,385
Everyone on the show
is incredibly talented.

987
00:40:35,386 --> 00:40:37,226
I want to be able to hold
my own against them.

988
00:40:38,156 --> 00:40:39,896
I'm going to...

989
00:40:40,326 --> 00:40:42,866
show you exactly how I made it this far...

990
00:40:44,766 --> 00:40:46,166
in the competition.

991
00:40:49,606 --> 00:40:52,206
Back Koo Young's Last Stage: 24H...

992
00:40:52,436 --> 00:40:54,176
begins now.

993
00:40:54,476 --> 00:40:56,376
Show us, Koo Young. Let's go.

994
00:40:57,476 --> 00:40:59,646
Ready, fight.

995
00:41:04,786 --> 00:41:05,786
I'm so nervous.

996
00:41:05,886 --> 00:41:07,455
His performance is risky.

997
00:41:07,456 --> 00:41:09,526
He could've played it safe.

998
00:41:09,756 --> 00:41:11,355
I think he can do it.

999
00:41:11,356 --> 00:41:13,596
I feel like this is a risk
he can definitely manage.

1000
00:41:13,796 --> 00:41:15,756
Anyway, he always
kills it when it's showtime.

1001
00:41:16,196 --> 00:41:18,042
(Team Back Koo Young's dancers
get ready for the performance.)

1002
00:41:18,066 --> 00:41:19,936
They're already bruised.

1003
00:41:21,636 --> 00:41:23,436
The starting formation is pretty cool.

1004
00:41:23,736 --> 00:41:25,065
I guess there will be a surprise.

1005
00:41:25,066 --> 00:41:26,376
Let's go!

1006
00:41:42,016 --> 00:41:43,626
I'll survive no matter what.

1007
00:41:47,496 --> 00:41:48,695
("Bruise and Poison," Bruises
are painful, but familiar to dancers.)

1008
00:41:48,696 --> 00:41:49,925
(Despite the bruises, dancers
keep dancing, drawn to the thrill.)

1009
00:41:49,926 --> 00:41:51,165
(Bruises go beyond their
body and into their heart.)

1010
00:41:51,166 --> 00:41:53,436
("Bruise and Poison")

1011
00:42:14,616 --> 00:42:15,756
He's going to show us.

1012
00:42:33,276 --> 00:42:34,306
HARIMU.

1013
00:42:39,176 --> 00:42:41,415
No one executes an
intense concept like this...

1014
00:42:41,416 --> 00:42:42,746
better than Koo Young.

1015
00:42:57,326 --> 00:42:59,166
The formation got
lopsided before he did that.

1016
00:42:59,796 --> 00:43:01,196
Gosh, that was clever.

1017
00:43:22,256 --> 00:43:23,655
- There it comes.
- I hope he doesn't get hurt.

1018
00:43:23,656 --> 00:43:24,986
Please.

1019
00:43:25,086 --> 00:43:26,126
Please.

1020
00:43:26,326 --> 00:43:27,856
Please pull this off, Koo Young.

1021
00:43:28,126 --> 00:43:29,596
I'll make it work no matter what.

1022
00:43:29,696 --> 00:43:32,326
I'll get up there even if I
crawl. I'll finish with the jump.

1023
00:43:32,996 --> 00:43:34,296
- Don't get hurt!
- Let's go!

1024
00:43:56,156 --> 00:43:58,186
There he is.

1025
00:43:58,426 --> 00:43:59,426
He's in the moment.

1026
00:43:59,726 --> 00:44:01,196
How did he make that work?

1027
00:44:01,756 --> 00:44:03,366
He did it. He pulled it off.

1028
00:44:05,866 --> 00:44:06,936
Let's go!

1029
00:44:46,906 --> 00:44:48,105
(Team Back Koo Young's dancers:
HARIMU, Nohwon, Park Sae Rim, )

1030
00:44:48,106 --> 00:44:49,652
(Yoon In Jeong, Eunhye,
HYEYEON, Jin Ye Chan, Lee Na Ra...)

1031
00:44:49,676 --> 00:44:50,846
My gosh. That was crazy.

1032
00:44:51,046 --> 00:44:52,176
People are going wild.

1033
00:44:52,446 --> 00:44:53,746
The stage direction...

1034
00:44:56,916 --> 00:44:58,016
He did so well.

1035
00:44:59,086 --> 00:45:00,786
He did it.

1036
00:45:06,326 --> 00:45:07,856
No way.

1037
00:45:10,026 --> 00:45:11,166
I made it work.

1038
00:45:11,796 --> 00:45:14,095
This is making me emotional.

1039
00:45:14,096 --> 00:45:16,706
I'm overwhelmed with emotions.

1040
00:45:17,266 --> 00:45:19,976
I've known him for so long.

1041
00:45:20,206 --> 00:45:21,975
The other dancers I met when I was young...

1042
00:45:21,976 --> 00:45:24,476
don't have much energy left
now that they're getting old.

1043
00:45:24,746 --> 00:45:26,915
But he's still in the
same place I met him first.

1044
00:45:26,916 --> 00:45:28,176
So I like that.

1045
00:45:28,416 --> 00:45:29,686
His dancing is just incredible.

1046
00:45:30,616 --> 00:45:32,015
Let's find out...

1047
00:45:32,016 --> 00:45:34,716
what the three judges
thought about his performance.

1048
00:45:34,758 --> 00:45:37,258
It's time to listen to their evaluations.

1049
00:45:37,828 --> 00:45:40,458
First of all, when I thought of purple,

1050
00:45:40,658 --> 00:45:42,828
bruises were the last
thing on my mind, honestly.

1051
00:45:43,098 --> 00:45:46,298
I started to get goosebumps when
you mentioned bruises and addiction.

1052
00:45:46,598 --> 00:45:49,567
The message and emotions
you wanted to deliver with purple...

1053
00:45:49,568 --> 00:45:51,808
clearly came through.

1054
00:45:52,108 --> 00:45:53,878
Right. His concept wasn't one-dimensional.

1055
00:45:54,258 --> 00:45:57,127
At the end, your body
was covered with bruises...

1056
00:45:57,128 --> 00:46:00,497
which nicely touched your
message about addiction.

1057
00:46:00,498 --> 00:46:01,568
I was truly impressed.

1058
00:46:02,188 --> 00:46:03,788
Amazing.

1059
00:46:06,558 --> 00:46:08,998
I'm hooked on this narrative you created.

1060
00:46:09,298 --> 00:46:13,738
It feels like my whole body
is also covered with bruises.

1061
00:46:13,968 --> 00:46:16,437
I could feel the pain too.

1062
00:46:16,438 --> 00:46:18,207
When the tempo changed,

1063
00:46:18,208 --> 00:46:20,708
you were addicted to the joy of dancing.

1064
00:46:20,908 --> 00:46:23,208
So it was not something you could control.

1065
00:46:23,448 --> 00:46:25,508
I'm sure everyone, including myself...

1066
00:46:25,778 --> 00:46:30,188
felt a similar emotional change
throughout your performance.

1067
00:46:30,236 --> 00:46:33,806
You only had 24 hours to pull this off.

1068
00:46:34,106 --> 00:46:35,826
And yet, you still wanted to achieve a lot.

1069
00:46:36,106 --> 00:46:38,545
(The chance of pulling
off the jump was very slim.)

1070
00:46:38,546 --> 00:46:39,816
"What if I mess it up again?"

1071
00:46:41,146 --> 00:46:42,716
I'll make it work.

1072
00:46:43,986 --> 00:46:45,146
I did it.

1073
00:46:45,616 --> 00:46:47,486
They went wild exactly
when I wanted them to.

1074
00:46:48,786 --> 00:46:52,826
I'd like to say that luckily, it
was a successful performance.

1075
00:46:52,986 --> 00:46:53,995
I did it.

1076
00:46:53,996 --> 00:46:56,926
It's rare for me to feel this
deep sense of achievement.

1077
00:46:57,066 --> 00:46:58,526
This is crazy. He's so tenacious.

1078
00:46:58,726 --> 00:47:01,236
Seriously. Koo Young has a spine of steel.

1079
00:47:01,466 --> 00:47:03,205
I knew that his tenacity...

1080
00:47:03,206 --> 00:47:05,236
would definitely shine in Last Stage.

1081
00:47:05,606 --> 00:47:07,406
High risk brings high return.

1082
00:47:07,606 --> 00:47:10,146
Since he managed a high
risk, he'll get a high return.

1083
00:47:10,406 --> 00:47:11,976
He might end up winning.

1084
00:47:12,646 --> 00:47:14,576
Your formations were varied too.

1085
00:47:14,716 --> 00:47:18,846
In my opinion, your formations
were quite experimental.

1086
00:47:19,016 --> 00:47:20,286
He was incredibly detailed.

1087
00:47:20,356 --> 00:47:21,415
So here was the formation.

1088
00:47:21,416 --> 00:47:23,302
And they were dancing, and
the formation got lopsided.

1089
00:47:23,326 --> 00:47:25,686
The moment we noticed that,
he did something in the corner.

1090
00:47:27,496 --> 00:47:29,055
This was a large-scale performance,

1091
00:47:29,056 --> 00:47:30,866
but I was still captivated by its elements.

1092
00:47:32,396 --> 00:47:33,466
He's so sharp.

1093
00:47:33,796 --> 00:47:35,536
His attention to detail.

1094
00:47:35,896 --> 00:47:38,182
This performance clearly showed
that he was on a different level.

1095
00:47:38,206 --> 00:47:40,246
We can't take this kind of
performance for granted.

1096
00:47:40,406 --> 00:47:41,976
I mean it.

1097
00:47:42,106 --> 00:47:45,276
We only get to see something
like this because he gave his all.

1098
00:47:46,476 --> 00:47:47,716
He must be getting emotional.

1099
00:47:48,446 --> 00:47:50,586
On that note, let's give
him a big round of applause.

1100
00:47:53,656 --> 00:47:55,256
She could relate...

1101
00:47:55,456 --> 00:47:56,886
to the story and concept.

1102
00:47:57,056 --> 00:47:58,785
It just felt so liberating.

1103
00:47:58,786 --> 00:48:00,356
Gosh, it was so freeing.

1104
00:48:00,496 --> 00:48:01,936
- Good work.
- Thank you. Well done.

1105
00:48:02,726 --> 00:48:03,996
Hyun Sung.

1106
00:48:04,466 --> 00:48:05,566
Thank you.

1107
00:48:06,096 --> 00:48:07,596
I'm so grateful to my dancers.

1108
00:48:08,596 --> 00:48:10,166
Despite everything,

1109
00:48:10,806 --> 00:48:13,006
no one can predict the results.

1110
00:48:13,576 --> 00:48:16,006
Seriously. I couldn't
be sure even to the end.

1111
00:48:16,476 --> 00:48:18,306
I can't afford to get eliminated now.

1112
00:48:18,746 --> 00:48:20,245
I have to make it to the
finals no matter what.

1113
00:48:20,246 --> 00:48:21,476
I mean it.

1114
00:48:22,576 --> 00:48:25,116
The next director of Last Stage is...

1115
00:48:25,616 --> 00:48:26,786
INGYOO.

1116
00:48:29,186 --> 00:48:30,386
INGYOO. Let's go.

1117
00:48:30,586 --> 00:48:32,656
He's debuting as a singer!

1118
00:48:34,856 --> 00:48:36,766
I've never seen him looking so sharp.

1119
00:48:37,266 --> 00:48:39,966
I've never seen him
with this low-key energy.

1120
00:48:40,396 --> 00:48:41,795
He's very calm today.

1121
00:48:41,796 --> 00:48:43,305
(INGYOO looks different than usual.)

1122
00:48:43,306 --> 00:48:44,536
Director INGYOO.

1123
00:48:44,736 --> 00:48:47,276
Your symbolic colour is green.

1124
00:48:47,506 --> 00:48:50,676
I'm curious to hear from you
what this colour means to you.

1125
00:48:51,446 --> 00:48:55,275
When I think of green,
nature, health, and recovery...

1126
00:48:55,276 --> 00:48:56,646
come to mind.

1127
00:48:56,916 --> 00:48:58,646
I tried to combine those images with mine.

1128
00:48:58,816 --> 00:49:00,986
Then I wanted to use my
energy and artistic vision...

1129
00:49:01,156 --> 00:49:02,916
to bring life to the people around me...

1130
00:49:03,056 --> 00:49:06,555
and help people recover.
That was the starting point...

1131
00:49:06,556 --> 00:49:07,695
of my concept.

1132
00:49:07,696 --> 00:49:09,195
When he said nature,
he didn't mean it literally.

1133
00:49:09,196 --> 00:49:10,926
He was focusing on life force.

1134
00:49:11,166 --> 00:49:14,296
Then I thought of the image, "Going Green."

1135
00:49:14,636 --> 00:49:16,295
As for the message I want
to convey with my colour,

1136
00:49:16,296 --> 00:49:19,535
it's about the intangible elements.

1137
00:49:19,536 --> 00:49:20,605
I expressed them in my lyrics.

1138
00:49:20,606 --> 00:49:22,706
"Raise your hand if you ever took a loss."

1139
00:49:23,006 --> 00:49:25,775
"I had been running from
the dark since I was a kid."

1140
00:49:25,776 --> 00:49:28,076
I was especially insecure
and anxious growing up.

1141
00:49:28,216 --> 00:49:31,845
After overcoming these
dark, anxiety-driven moments,

1142
00:49:31,846 --> 00:49:33,085
I became who I am now.

1143
00:49:33,086 --> 00:49:34,916
Now, I'm leading my own team.

1144
00:49:35,116 --> 00:49:38,085
We inspire each other
and exchange good energy.

1145
00:49:38,086 --> 00:49:41,796
I think this is "Going Green"
in terms of emotional healing.

1146
00:49:42,426 --> 00:49:44,595
I incorporated my identity
and WE DEM BOYZ...

1147
00:49:44,596 --> 00:49:46,566
into the lyrics and finished the track.

1148
00:49:47,036 --> 00:49:50,236
Why am I holding the microphone?

1149
00:49:50,436 --> 00:49:51,606
Because I need to sing.

1150
00:49:52,066 --> 00:49:54,736
Give me the propolis spray.

1151
00:49:55,536 --> 00:49:56,976
(Spraying)

1152
00:49:57,346 --> 00:49:58,476
Yes, sir.

1153
00:49:59,146 --> 00:50:01,576
Actually, I started to
make music with a band.

1154
00:50:01,776 --> 00:50:03,315
I love music...

1155
00:50:03,316 --> 00:50:04,916
and singing too.

1156
00:50:05,046 --> 00:50:06,855
I incorporated my
real story into the lyrics.

1157
00:50:06,856 --> 00:50:09,555
I thought delivering this
message through my own vocals...

1158
00:50:09,556 --> 00:50:11,426
suited my concept of "Going Green" better.

1159
00:50:11,656 --> 00:50:13,025
I don't think they'll believe it at first.

1160
00:50:13,026 --> 00:50:14,556
"What's going on? Is this real?"

1161
00:50:14,656 --> 00:50:15,926
He's wearing an in-ear monitor.

1162
00:50:16,026 --> 00:50:17,495
He's a dancer. He should warm up his body.

1163
00:50:17,496 --> 00:50:19,336
- Why is he warming up his voice?
- Seriously.

1164
00:50:19,396 --> 00:50:22,195
I noticed that it sounded much better...

1165
00:50:22,196 --> 00:50:23,806
when it was empty.

1166
00:50:24,336 --> 00:50:26,906
Could you set up the lighting now?

1167
00:50:27,406 --> 00:50:29,582
- Do you want the prism to be green?
- Green? Let's go with that.

1168
00:50:29,606 --> 00:50:31,746
Let's go with green for the spider too.

1169
00:50:32,006 --> 00:50:33,915
I used LED screens and stage lights...

1170
00:50:33,916 --> 00:50:36,015
to make sure my performance
didn't fall short visually.

1171
00:50:36,016 --> 00:50:38,415
I tried to fill the stage with green...

1172
00:50:38,416 --> 00:50:40,376
and focused on that while
staging my performance.

1173
00:50:40,616 --> 00:50:43,456
The theme of my performance is...

1174
00:50:43,556 --> 00:50:45,055
"Going Green."

1175
00:50:45,056 --> 00:50:46,955
But the core theme
of that would be rebirth.

1176
00:50:46,956 --> 00:50:48,096
I'm born again.

1177
00:50:48,326 --> 00:50:51,495
I do think this debut performance
is very meaningful to me...

1178
00:50:51,496 --> 00:50:52,766
and to the dance industry.

1179
00:50:52,926 --> 00:50:55,665
I projected a pulsing heartbeat
to symbolize my rebirth.

1180
00:50:55,666 --> 00:50:58,005
With a glitch, it's going to
change into a sound wave.

1181
00:50:58,006 --> 00:51:00,675
I did produce the music.

1182
00:51:00,676 --> 00:51:02,275
Then it ends with the Earth.

1183
00:51:02,276 --> 00:51:03,982
The message is that I want
to do good for the world.

1184
00:51:04,006 --> 00:51:07,046
I pulled out everything in my
arsenal for this performance.

1185
00:51:07,676 --> 00:51:10,115
(The seats are filling up.)

1186
00:51:10,116 --> 00:51:12,085
It's finally happening.
I'm going to sing...

1187
00:51:12,086 --> 00:51:14,216
and dance in front of an audience?

1188
00:51:14,716 --> 00:51:16,016
This will be my debut?

1189
00:51:16,556 --> 00:51:18,826
Then I suddenly forgot my lyrics.

1190
00:51:19,126 --> 00:51:20,156
I'm doomed.

1191
00:51:20,596 --> 00:51:22,655
If I mess up the lyrics...

1192
00:51:22,656 --> 00:51:24,536
I mean, this is my
debut if you think about it.

1193
00:51:24,996 --> 00:51:27,076
(He starts practising
backstage at the last minute.)

1194
00:51:27,336 --> 00:51:29,266
Things got intense. It was an emergency.

1195
00:51:29,496 --> 00:51:31,935
I tried to re-memorize the lyrics I forgot.

1196
00:51:31,936 --> 00:51:34,036
I had to focus like crazy to do that.

1197
00:51:34,876 --> 00:51:36,845
(Practising one last
time with the water bottle)

1198
00:51:36,846 --> 00:51:38,375
Can I get the propolis spray now?

1199
00:51:38,376 --> 00:51:39,496
- The propolis spray?
- Yes.

1200
00:51:39,876 --> 00:51:41,516
- Let's do this.
- Let's go.

1201
00:51:41,776 --> 00:51:42,946
Let's go.

1202
00:51:43,586 --> 00:51:45,245
- You got this.
- Let's go.

1203
00:51:45,246 --> 00:51:46,246
- Good luck.
- Let's do this.

1204
00:51:46,247 --> 00:51:48,756
Singing the song live will be my risk.

1205
00:51:49,316 --> 00:51:50,636
I'll make it work no matter what.

1206
00:51:51,256 --> 00:51:53,156
He's going for it despite the risk.

1207
00:51:53,496 --> 00:51:54,796
He seems very nervous.

1208
00:51:55,256 --> 00:51:58,566
You're about to perform now.
Tell us the kind of determination...

1209
00:51:58,826 --> 00:52:00,506
that went into preparing this performance.

1210
00:52:01,266 --> 00:52:04,405
This is called Last Stage.

1211
00:52:04,406 --> 00:52:08,976
So when I thought about my darkest time...

1212
00:52:09,036 --> 00:52:11,475
and that it was over for me,

1213
00:52:11,476 --> 00:52:12,806
my team,

1214
00:52:13,446 --> 00:52:16,516
my art, and my life came to mind.

1215
00:52:17,046 --> 00:52:19,286
- On that note...
- That's quite poetic.

1216
00:52:19,416 --> 00:52:23,525
On that note, I'd like to
dedicate the energy of my life...

1217
00:52:23,526 --> 00:52:25,886
to my team and all the art I put out.

1218
00:52:29,296 --> 00:52:31,296
- Dedicate it.
- This is his life.

1219
00:52:31,666 --> 00:52:33,196
(INGYOO, let's go.)

1220
00:52:33,666 --> 00:52:36,396
INGYOO's Last Stage: 24H...

1221
00:52:36,706 --> 00:52:38,706
begins now.

1222
00:52:39,206 --> 00:52:41,936
Make some noise!

1223
00:52:43,906 --> 00:52:45,876
- Ready, fight.
- Let's go.

1224
00:52:46,246 --> 00:52:48,146
- Let's go.
- Fight.

1225
00:52:48,546 --> 00:52:52,015
If you think about it, WE
DEM BOYZ has a raw edge.

1226
00:52:52,016 --> 00:52:54,186
So green might go well
with his performance.

1227
00:52:54,756 --> 00:52:57,725
(A rather raw cheer)

1228
00:52:57,726 --> 00:52:58,826
Let's go, WE DEM BOYZ!

1229
00:52:59,956 --> 00:53:01,355
(WE DEM BOYZ enter in black)

1230
00:53:01,356 --> 00:53:03,156
They're a little scary, though.

1231
00:53:03,996 --> 00:53:05,726
They have that scary vitality.

1232
00:53:06,226 --> 00:53:07,566
The chemistry.

1233
00:53:07,696 --> 00:53:09,265
Even their outfits have that "Matrix" vibe,

1234
00:53:09,266 --> 00:53:11,065
just throwing on some leather.

1235
00:53:11,066 --> 00:53:12,166
I'm excited.

1236
00:53:13,976 --> 00:53:15,575
It really looks like sunset.

1237
00:53:15,576 --> 00:53:17,676
The lighting's gorgeous. Like a sunset.

1238
00:53:18,276 --> 00:53:19,475
They really are one team.

1239
00:53:19,476 --> 00:53:21,476
Their aura as a team is so powerful.

1240
00:53:22,046 --> 00:53:23,515
Where's INGYOO?

1241
00:53:23,516 --> 00:53:25,316
Is he in the back? Is he coming out later?

1242
00:53:27,316 --> 00:53:28,355
Thank you.

1243
00:53:28,356 --> 00:53:30,085
(INGYOO takes the stage with a mic)

1244
00:53:30,086 --> 00:53:32,356
There he is!

1245
00:53:34,696 --> 00:53:36,696
Make some noise!

1246
00:53:36,766 --> 00:53:39,666
Yeah! Make some noise! What's up!

1247
00:53:39,796 --> 00:53:41,766
(What's going on?)

1248
00:53:41,866 --> 00:53:42,965
(What?)

1249
00:53:42,966 --> 00:53:44,436
I guess he's performing with a mic.

1250
00:53:45,306 --> 00:53:47,476
(Let's go!)

1251
00:53:47,536 --> 00:53:48,836
Part of the show?

1252
00:53:48,906 --> 00:53:50,675
- He can rap?
- With a mic.

1253
00:53:50,676 --> 00:53:51,776
Really?

1254
00:53:52,046 --> 00:53:54,045
When I say, "Bring the bounce..."

1255
00:53:54,046 --> 00:53:57,246
(Everyone bounces)

1256
00:53:57,816 --> 00:54:00,255
(Even the judges react on instinct)

1257
00:54:00,256 --> 00:54:01,556
Do that, okay?

1258
00:54:01,986 --> 00:54:03,085
Promise!

1259
00:54:03,086 --> 00:54:04,286
(No worries)

1260
00:54:05,526 --> 00:54:06,895
That presence!

1261
00:54:06,896 --> 00:54:08,956
What a stunning silhouette.

1262
00:54:09,126 --> 00:54:12,765
I want to show our
purest, most joyful selves.

1263
00:54:12,766 --> 00:54:13,936
Me and WE DEM BOYZ.

1264
00:54:16,396 --> 00:54:18,135
(INGYOO's signature green
symbolizes life, healing and growth)

1265
00:54:18,136 --> 00:54:20,452
("Going Green" spreads his energy
to revitalize and cleanse the world)

1266
00:54:20,476 --> 00:54:23,746
("Going G" by Team INGYOO)

1267
00:54:24,046 --> 00:54:26,175
(Excited)

1268
00:54:26,176 --> 00:54:27,675
That shadow looks amazing.

1269
00:54:27,676 --> 00:54:29,576
That heartbeat!

1270
00:54:29,616 --> 00:54:30,786
That's incredible.

1271
00:54:31,886 --> 00:54:32,986
There he is!

1272
00:54:34,986 --> 00:54:36,516
He's such a good dancer.

1273
00:54:42,926 --> 00:54:44,426
That's unreal.

1274
00:54:52,006 --> 00:54:53,576
You're right.

1275
00:54:58,546 --> 00:55:00,445
It's like we're at "M COUNTDOWN"!

1276
00:55:00,446 --> 00:55:01,546
Yes!

1277
00:55:02,416 --> 00:55:04,385
His dancing is on another level.

1278
00:55:04,386 --> 00:55:05,515
They're so in sync.

1279
00:55:05,516 --> 00:55:06,686
That's got flavour!

1280
00:55:09,656 --> 00:55:11,456
- Let's go!
- Here we go!

1281
00:55:16,656 --> 00:55:18,426
(Startled)

1282
00:55:18,796 --> 00:55:20,536
Wait, he can sing well too?

1283
00:55:50,056 --> 00:55:51,965
He's really living his dream.

1284
00:55:51,966 --> 00:55:53,866
Let's get you on a music show.

1285
00:55:59,566 --> 00:56:02,376
He's a singer who can really dance.

1286
00:56:07,846 --> 00:56:09,316
(The waiting room bounces too.)

1287
00:56:23,426 --> 00:56:25,766
Everyone's loving this performance.

1288
00:56:29,166 --> 00:56:30,166
Let's go!

1289
00:56:37,906 --> 00:56:39,876
What? That wasn't there before!

1290
00:56:40,046 --> 00:56:41,046
(A surprise jam session)

1291
00:56:42,476 --> 00:56:44,216
(On their feet before they know it)

1292
00:56:45,116 --> 00:56:46,585
(Min Ho)

1293
00:56:46,586 --> 00:56:49,356
(Tae Min)

1294
00:56:52,626 --> 00:56:55,596
(LIL LAW)

1295
00:57:02,896 --> 00:57:04,435
(Right up their alley)

1296
00:57:04,436 --> 00:57:06,935
This is WE DEM BOYZ. Make some noise!

1297
00:57:06,936 --> 00:57:08,205
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

1298
00:57:08,206 --> 00:57:09,635
(National tour concert information)

1299
00:57:09,636 --> 00:57:11,075
They're one team.

1300
00:57:11,076 --> 00:57:12,446
(Team INGYOO Dancers)

1301
00:57:14,646 --> 00:57:15,945
You should've just jumped in.

1302
00:57:15,946 --> 00:57:18,516
I know, right? Everything!

1303
00:57:19,446 --> 00:57:20,455
That was fun.

1304
00:57:20,456 --> 00:57:22,156
They got people moving.

1305
00:57:23,016 --> 00:57:26,126
That was great. Everyone had a blast.

1306
00:57:26,286 --> 00:57:28,496
That was such a bold choice.

1307
00:57:29,096 --> 00:57:30,825
Could anyone here...

1308
00:57:30,826 --> 00:57:31,826
do that? I don't think so.

1309
00:57:31,827 --> 00:57:33,766
Just being able to pull that off...

1310
00:57:34,336 --> 00:57:35,666
is truly amazing.

1311
00:57:35,836 --> 00:57:36,936
Honestly,

1312
00:57:37,206 --> 00:57:40,936
I think it could divide opinions.

1313
00:57:41,036 --> 00:57:42,676
This was just... What?

1314
00:57:43,236 --> 00:57:44,345
I didn't expect that.

1315
00:57:44,346 --> 00:57:48,316
I'm not sure it fits the judging criteria.

1316
00:57:49,346 --> 00:57:50,986
- It's tough.
- Yes.

1317
00:57:51,016 --> 00:57:54,455
The other teams' performances...

1318
00:57:54,456 --> 00:57:56,085
were built around visual concepts,

1319
00:57:56,086 --> 00:57:58,385
but INGYOO focused on the essence of dance.

1320
00:57:58,386 --> 00:58:01,496
That's what makes this so difficult.

1321
00:58:01,726 --> 00:58:03,356
It's one approach or the other.

1322
00:58:03,626 --> 00:58:05,396
What will they choose? I'm really curious.

1323
00:58:06,026 --> 00:58:09,666
Let's hear the Fight Judges' comments now.

1324
00:58:09,766 --> 00:58:13,665
This is my first time seeing INGYOO.

1325
00:58:13,666 --> 00:58:15,506
And he's holding a mic?

1326
00:58:15,676 --> 00:58:18,275
Does anything go on Directors' War?

1327
00:58:18,276 --> 00:58:19,376
Incredible.

1328
00:58:19,606 --> 00:58:22,915
How do I put it? Thinking outside the box?

1329
00:58:22,916 --> 00:58:25,985
Doing what no one else imagined...

1330
00:58:25,986 --> 00:58:29,015
without being afraid...

1331
00:58:29,016 --> 00:58:32,455
and not drawing lines
between director, artist...

1332
00:58:32,456 --> 00:58:34,825
and entertainer...

1333
00:58:34,826 --> 00:58:36,755
is what I call real swag.

1334
00:58:36,756 --> 00:58:41,096
If my crew had been here,
I'm sure they would've...

1335
00:58:41,266 --> 00:58:43,436
joined in at that final cypher.

1336
00:58:43,696 --> 00:58:47,305
It's hard to be that
honest onstage, isn't it?

1337
00:58:47,306 --> 00:58:49,075
And in just 24 hours...

1338
00:58:49,076 --> 00:58:52,605
Rather than just sending
energy out from the stage,

1339
00:58:52,606 --> 00:58:55,775
to pull us in with an
invitation to dance...

1340
00:58:55,776 --> 00:58:58,485
I know how hard that is,

1341
00:58:58,486 --> 00:59:01,655
so doing all that in 24
hours is really impressive.

1342
00:59:01,656 --> 00:59:04,225
Thank you so much for inviting us.

1343
00:59:04,226 --> 00:59:05,585
But...

1344
00:59:05,586 --> 00:59:09,795
what I'm still struggling with is...

1345
00:59:09,796 --> 00:59:13,495
how this choice, which
was so true to you, INGYOO,

1346
00:59:13,496 --> 00:59:17,305
stacks up against the other two teams.

1347
00:59:17,306 --> 00:59:19,166
I'm still thinking it over.

1348
00:59:19,436 --> 00:59:21,236
You've made this agonizing for me.

1349
00:59:21,936 --> 00:59:22,976
I know.

1350
00:59:23,576 --> 00:59:26,075
- He's definitely an icon, right?
- He's an icon.

1351
00:59:26,076 --> 00:59:28,745
He's truly remarkable.

1352
00:59:28,746 --> 00:59:30,545
The quality speaks for itself.

1353
00:59:30,546 --> 00:59:31,986
We all got up on our feet.

1354
00:59:32,246 --> 00:59:33,885
What I felt was...

1355
00:59:33,886 --> 00:59:36,755
he wasn't trying to force a meaning.

1356
00:59:36,756 --> 00:59:38,625
Just what he loves...

1357
00:59:38,626 --> 00:59:40,155
and what he wants to do.

1358
00:59:40,156 --> 00:59:42,855
This is so pure.

1359
00:59:42,856 --> 00:59:45,295
This is the essence. That's how it felt.

1360
00:59:45,296 --> 00:59:47,665
But at the same time, INGYOO...

1361
00:59:47,666 --> 00:59:50,095
has given everyone watching...

1362
00:59:50,096 --> 00:59:51,736
something to think about.

1363
00:59:51,906 --> 00:59:55,005
When we think of Directors' War,

1364
00:59:55,006 --> 00:59:57,775
and the scope of directing,

1365
00:59:57,776 --> 01:00:00,445
there's a lot more to think about now.

1366
01:00:00,446 --> 01:00:03,885
So we really need to
give that some thought.

1367
01:00:03,886 --> 01:00:05,345
In a way, this team...

1368
01:00:05,346 --> 01:00:06,415
took on an extra challenge.

1369
01:00:06,416 --> 01:00:09,155
- You had to learn the lyrics too.
- I had to learn the lyrics.

1370
01:00:09,156 --> 01:00:12,325
I want to thank you for
taking on this challenge.

1371
01:00:12,326 --> 01:00:14,526
This energy!

1372
01:00:14,926 --> 01:00:16,855
(Fully recharged)

1373
01:00:16,856 --> 01:00:19,226
- That was his debut performance.
- His debut performance.

1374
01:00:19,496 --> 01:00:21,435
Getting someone to dance...

1375
01:00:21,436 --> 01:00:23,906
is so rewarding and fun for me.

1376
01:00:24,966 --> 01:00:28,776
My team brings such a great vibe,

1377
01:00:29,336 --> 01:00:33,005
and this performance
combines everything I do best,

1378
01:00:33,006 --> 01:00:35,446
so I do think I might
have a shot at winning.

1379
01:00:36,916 --> 01:00:41,155
Our long "Street World
Fighter: Directors' War" journey...

1380
01:00:41,156 --> 01:00:43,856
is finally nearing its last stage.

1381
01:00:44,126 --> 01:00:46,686
The theme given to
today's three directors...

1382
01:00:46,926 --> 01:00:49,556
was a colour to symbolize each of them.

1383
01:00:50,326 --> 01:00:52,295
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

1384
01:00:52,296 --> 01:00:53,296
(Title Sequence Film Mission)

1385
01:00:53,297 --> 01:00:55,535
Through countless missions
and moments of choice,

1386
01:00:55,536 --> 01:00:56,872
(K-pop Solo Artist Direct Mission)

1387
01:00:56,896 --> 01:01:00,006
they've each shown their
true colours in their own way.

1388
01:01:00,136 --> 01:01:04,975
With BABYZOO and Kasper
already through to the finals,

1389
01:01:04,976 --> 01:01:07,315
there are only...

1390
01:01:07,316 --> 01:01:09,016
two spots left to join them.

1391
01:01:09,216 --> 01:01:10,646
I did what I prepared.

1392
01:01:10,886 --> 01:01:12,885
The gestures, expressions and directing...

1393
01:01:12,886 --> 01:01:15,015
all came together well,

1394
01:01:15,016 --> 01:01:16,016
so I have no regrets.

1395
01:01:16,316 --> 01:01:19,285
I think I showed all my colours.

1396
01:01:19,286 --> 01:01:21,295
I think it was a truly perfect performance,

1397
01:01:21,296 --> 01:01:22,656
so I'll survive.

1398
01:01:23,396 --> 01:01:24,565
(Sigh)

1399
01:01:24,566 --> 01:01:27,565
No one could predict the outcome,

1400
01:01:27,566 --> 01:01:29,696
so I was incredibly nervous.

1401
01:01:31,036 --> 01:01:32,765
I pulled off what I wanted to do,

1402
01:01:32,766 --> 01:01:36,205
but I really don't know
how the judges assessed it.

1403
01:01:36,206 --> 01:01:38,605
I kept wondering what they'd decided.

1404
01:01:38,606 --> 01:01:40,616
They did seem to be thinking hard.

1405
01:01:41,016 --> 01:01:42,415
My judging criterion...

1406
01:01:42,416 --> 01:01:45,285
My judging criterion...

1407
01:01:45,286 --> 01:01:48,086
isn't how well the director did.

1408
01:01:48,256 --> 01:01:50,415
If only the director stands out,

1409
01:01:50,416 --> 01:01:52,626
it becomes a one-person contest.

1410
01:01:52,726 --> 01:01:56,696
I judge the overall quality...

1411
01:01:56,896 --> 01:01:58,666
of the work they created together.

1412
01:01:58,766 --> 01:02:01,036
In a competition,

1413
01:02:01,066 --> 01:02:04,236
what you choose as your weapon...

1414
01:02:04,536 --> 01:02:05,665
- really matters.
- Right.

1415
01:02:05,666 --> 01:02:07,575
We look at that...

1416
01:02:07,576 --> 01:02:09,482
- to decide who wins.
- Whether they used a shield...

1417
01:02:09,506 --> 01:02:11,045
- or went for a strike...
- Right.

1418
01:02:11,046 --> 01:02:12,946
- is what we have to judge.
- Right.

1419
01:02:13,576 --> 01:02:15,446
Honestly,

1420
01:02:15,516 --> 01:02:19,385
- all three were so polished.
- They were incredible.

1421
01:02:19,386 --> 01:02:20,785
The quality was just unbelievable.

1422
01:02:20,786 --> 01:02:23,485
To do all that in just 24 hours...

1423
01:02:23,486 --> 01:02:25,525
- How is that even possible?
- Not one left me thinking, "What?"

1424
01:02:25,526 --> 01:02:29,426
It's really not a question
of anyone doing poorly...

1425
01:02:29,496 --> 01:02:32,766
If we're just looking at
how they used the stage,

1426
01:02:32,896 --> 01:02:35,066
- BADA comes first in that regard.
- Right.

1427
01:02:35,496 --> 01:02:36,535
- But...
- Right.

1428
01:02:36,536 --> 01:02:37,736
But...

1429
01:02:37,806 --> 01:02:40,735
in terms of the theme,

1430
01:02:40,736 --> 01:02:42,006
I'd rank Koo Young first.

1431
01:02:42,236 --> 01:02:44,675
For how honestly they
expressed the essence of dance...

1432
01:02:44,676 --> 01:02:46,805
and how daring they were,

1433
01:02:46,806 --> 01:02:48,515
INGYOO comes first.

1434
01:02:48,516 --> 01:02:49,975
Exactly.

1435
01:02:49,976 --> 01:02:53,316
They each took a different
approach to winning,

1436
01:02:53,586 --> 01:02:54,786
so it's a tough decision.

1437
01:02:54,886 --> 01:02:57,016
(Sigh)

1438
01:02:57,086 --> 01:03:00,626
All three have brought their
colours to countless performances.

1439
01:03:00,726 --> 01:03:03,325
Two of them will become finalists...

1440
01:03:03,326 --> 01:03:05,426
and take the final stage.

1441
01:03:05,726 --> 01:03:08,466
One will fall at the final hurdle...

1442
01:03:08,536 --> 01:03:11,306
and end their journey on this show.

1443
01:03:11,566 --> 01:03:14,275
We're just one step away from the finals.

1444
01:03:14,276 --> 01:03:17,846
I hope I survive this inferno.

1445
01:03:18,476 --> 01:03:20,815
So please...

1446
01:03:20,816 --> 01:03:22,915
I can't be eliminated now.

1447
01:03:22,916 --> 01:03:24,485
I have to reach the finals.

1448
01:03:24,486 --> 01:03:25,846
No matter what.

1449
01:03:26,746 --> 01:03:28,015
I had so much fun performing.

1450
01:03:28,016 --> 01:03:29,986
Regardless of win or lose, I'm satisfied.

1451
01:03:30,516 --> 01:03:33,526
The directors who survived
the final Last Stage: 24H...

1452
01:03:33,626 --> 01:03:36,296
and earned their places as finalists are...

1453
01:03:36,656 --> 01:03:37,995
Who will the two be?

1454
01:03:37,996 --> 01:03:39,265
Who will it be?

1455
01:03:39,266 --> 01:03:41,296
Any of them could advance, right?

1456
01:03:41,566 --> 01:03:43,766
You just never know with Last Stage.

1457
01:03:45,266 --> 01:03:46,535
Director...

1458
01:03:46,536 --> 01:03:50,076
(Who is the first finalist?)

1459
01:03:51,006 --> 01:03:52,205
It's BADA.

1460
01:03:52,206 --> 01:03:53,906
(BADA advances to the finals)

1461
01:03:57,276 --> 01:03:58,846
- Congrats, BADA.
- Thank you.

1462
01:03:59,386 --> 01:04:00,446
Congratulations.

1463
01:04:02,556 --> 01:04:04,286
Good luck.

1464
01:04:05,026 --> 01:04:06,285
Good luck.

1465
01:04:06,286 --> 01:04:09,926
(BADA becomes the first finalist.)

1466
01:04:12,026 --> 01:04:15,465
How you interpret the theme
changes the whole performance.

1467
01:04:15,466 --> 01:04:17,135
She chose "Boss" as her theme...

1468
01:04:17,136 --> 01:04:19,235
- and had a clear concept.
- Right.

1469
01:04:19,236 --> 01:04:21,305
She played to her strengths...

1470
01:04:21,306 --> 01:04:23,205
to show what she does best...

1471
01:04:23,206 --> 01:04:24,806
and brought out her star quality.

1472
01:04:24,876 --> 01:04:26,905
In terms of how they used the stage,

1473
01:04:26,906 --> 01:04:29,616
BADA was the only one to
move away from center stage.

1474
01:04:29,746 --> 01:04:32,045
It was so cohesive and clear,
you could see it right away.

1475
01:04:32,046 --> 01:04:34,045
The transitions were clean.

1476
01:04:34,046 --> 01:04:36,715
It felt like she showed only
what she wanted us to see.

1477
01:04:36,716 --> 01:04:39,785
When I joined Street World
Fighter: Directors' War,

1478
01:04:39,786 --> 01:04:41,895
this survival competition,

1479
01:04:41,896 --> 01:04:44,225
I just wanted to reach the finals.

1480
01:04:44,226 --> 01:04:46,666
That was my mindset.

1481
01:04:46,796 --> 01:04:48,335
I'm so grateful...

1482
01:04:48,336 --> 01:04:50,865
for this wonderful
opportunity to reach the finals.

1483
01:04:50,866 --> 01:04:51,905
It's such an honour.

1484
01:04:51,906 --> 01:04:53,335
The finals have been my dream,

1485
01:04:53,336 --> 01:04:55,135
and I'll work hard to prepare.

1486
01:04:55,136 --> 01:04:56,236
Thank you.

1487
01:04:58,946 --> 01:04:59,975
Well done.

1488
01:04:59,976 --> 01:05:01,245
You're amazing.

1489
01:05:01,246 --> 01:05:02,276
(A tight hug)

1490
01:05:02,716 --> 01:05:03,716
You've worked so hard.

1491
01:05:03,717 --> 01:05:05,146
I'm going to cry again.

1492
01:05:06,886 --> 01:05:09,215
Just being able to reach the finals...

1493
01:05:09,216 --> 01:05:12,326
makes me feel like one lucky girl.

1494
01:05:12,386 --> 01:05:13,926
And I think...

1495
01:05:14,426 --> 01:05:16,355
I could rise to the occasion...

1496
01:05:16,356 --> 01:05:18,365
and make the most of that luck...

1497
01:05:18,366 --> 01:05:20,295
because I had the skills...

1498
01:05:20,296 --> 01:05:21,665
to back it up.

1499
01:05:21,666 --> 01:05:22,935
In this game of Russian roulette,

1500
01:05:22,936 --> 01:05:25,666
I think the bullet missed me.

1501
01:05:26,106 --> 01:05:27,705
There's just...

1502
01:05:27,706 --> 01:05:28,906
one spot left in the finals.

1503
01:05:29,136 --> 01:05:32,706
One will claim that final spot,

1504
01:05:32,976 --> 01:05:35,775
while the other, with
the finals within reach,

1505
01:05:35,776 --> 01:05:38,586
will end their journey here today.

1506
01:05:38,946 --> 01:05:40,315
Koo Young looks so nervous.

1507
01:05:40,316 --> 01:05:41,956
Koo Young is really nervous.

1508
01:05:42,516 --> 01:05:45,056
I think I was hoping
Koo Young would make it.

1509
01:05:45,586 --> 01:05:48,756
Making it past Last Stage: 24H,

1510
01:05:48,996 --> 01:05:51,825
the director claiming the
last spot in the finals is...

1511
01:05:51,826 --> 01:05:54,165
Directors' War is about
showcasing your directing.

1512
01:05:54,166 --> 01:05:56,395
I showed more range as a director.

1513
01:05:56,396 --> 01:05:57,936
I'd say it's really 50-50.

1514
01:05:58,236 --> 01:06:00,936
Please, let it be Back Koo Young.

1515
01:06:01,536 --> 01:06:02,636
Director...

1516
01:06:04,106 --> 01:06:06,005
(The director advancing to the finals)

1517
01:06:06,006 --> 01:06:07,445
Back Koo Young.

1518
01:06:07,446 --> 01:06:10,446
(Back Koo Young advances to the finals.)

1519
01:06:11,416 --> 01:06:12,686
You did great, INGYOO.

1520
01:06:13,486 --> 01:06:14,616
Thank you.

1521
01:06:20,786 --> 01:06:24,296
Back Koo Young. Maybe he's the top.

1522
01:06:24,396 --> 01:06:29,265
He directed it as a complete work...

1523
01:06:29,266 --> 01:06:32,166
and seemed to look after everyone.

1524
01:06:32,236 --> 01:06:33,735
The dancing was great, too,

1525
01:06:33,736 --> 01:06:36,135
but the meaning he gave
it and his interpretation...

1526
01:06:36,136 --> 01:06:38,205
were just brilliant.

1527
01:06:38,206 --> 01:06:39,945
When he linked purple to bruises,

1528
01:06:39,946 --> 01:06:41,546
I thought, "Why didn't I see that?"

1529
01:06:41,616 --> 01:06:44,515
- "That's what I was looking for!"
- Right.

1530
01:06:44,516 --> 01:06:46,915
It makes you realise, "I
wish I'd thought of that."

1531
01:06:46,916 --> 01:06:49,686
That's real creativity.

1532
01:06:49,956 --> 01:06:51,725
Like an "Aha!" moment.

1533
01:06:51,726 --> 01:06:53,726
- Everyone hears it and goes, "Aha!"
- Right.

1534
01:06:54,256 --> 01:06:58,325
The two who shared this Last Stage with me,

1535
01:06:58,326 --> 01:07:00,325
INGYOO and BADA...

1536
01:07:00,326 --> 01:07:02,495
You worked so hard. Thanks to you,

1537
01:07:02,496 --> 01:07:05,135
I got to see amazing performances,

1538
01:07:05,136 --> 01:07:06,335
which made me really happy.

1539
01:07:06,336 --> 01:07:07,975
I feel like my dream came true,

1540
01:07:07,976 --> 01:07:09,706
so I'm thrilled.

1541
01:07:10,036 --> 01:07:12,646
I won't let you down,

1542
01:07:12,746 --> 01:07:14,976
and I'll give it my all...

1543
01:07:15,616 --> 01:07:17,946
to show you my best. Thank you.

1544
01:07:21,256 --> 01:07:22,816
I was so happy.

1545
01:07:23,086 --> 01:07:24,625
The finals...

1546
01:07:24,626 --> 01:07:26,925
I wanted to get there so badly.

1547
01:07:26,926 --> 01:07:29,026
I'd once come so close to the finals...

1548
01:07:29,056 --> 01:07:30,826
only to be crushed.

1549
01:07:31,226 --> 01:07:33,566
You have no idea how much I cried.

1550
01:07:36,696 --> 01:07:39,606
That feeling is etched in my memory,

1551
01:07:39,806 --> 01:07:42,805
but I felt I'd finally overcome it.

1552
01:07:42,806 --> 01:07:44,845
In Last Stage, I proved...

1553
01:07:44,846 --> 01:07:47,576
that I have what it
takes to reach the finals.

1554
01:07:49,916 --> 01:07:53,786
In the finals, I want to prove...

1555
01:07:54,656 --> 01:07:57,826
that Back Koo Young, the
director, has what it takes to win.

1556
01:07:57,886 --> 01:08:00,556
I'll make sure of it.

1557
01:08:01,456 --> 01:08:03,625
Sadly, this means...

1558
01:08:03,626 --> 01:08:06,566
Director INGYOO's journey ends here.

1559
01:08:07,696 --> 01:08:09,766
His colour got lost.

1560
01:08:10,296 --> 01:08:12,666
With BADA and Koo Young,

1561
01:08:12,736 --> 01:08:15,376
